            <ArticleTitle>Pulsed radiofrequency modulation for lingual neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e4-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjoms.2011.06.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pulsed radiofrequency modulation (PRM) is a minimally invasive procedure that has been used successfully to treat neuropathic pain. Its use to treat lingual neuralgia has not to our knowledge been described previously, and we report a case.</AbstractText>
